{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1786504421,"nonce":"Lothz3X/l4Tl3ALoAyQnVyaBZ9A=","target":"b2e4e18d066de42795555396d82bf2b5531dfea40e918a9bb09a52b15e7d1feb","message":"**What is wrong.** `deleteSource`, the handler for `DELETE /api/v1/sources/{id}`, performs two writes to two modules' tables in two separate transactions. `internal/sources/api/sources.go:309-318`:\n\n```go\nif err := rt.registry.SoftDelete(r.Context(), scope, id); err != nil {\n\thttpx.WriteProblem(w, r, err)\n\treturn\n}\nif rt.tokens != nil {\n\tif err := rt.tokens.RevokeIngestTokens(r.Context(), scope, id); err != nil {\n\t\thttpx.WriteProblem(w, r, err)\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n}\n```\n\nBoth calls take `r.Context()`. Per CONTEXT.md §5 rule 9 — *\"Transactions travel in `ctx` (`db.FromContext`). There are no `WithTx(tx)` method variants.\"* — a bare request context carries no transaction, so each call commits on its own. The `UnitOfWork` port that would make them one is already declared in this package, already injected, and already used by the two neighbouring handlers.\n\n**The demonstration.** `SoftDelete` writes `alert_sources`; `RevokeIngestTokens` writes identity's `api_tokens`. If the first commits and the second fails, the source is soft-deleted and its ingest token is still live — the webhook endpoint keeps authenticating and keeps accepting pushes for a source the operator has been told is gone. The handler answers 5xx, so the operator has no signal about which half landed, and there is no reconciliation pass that would later revoke the orphaned token.\n\nTwo doc-comments in this package name this exact failure. `internal/sources/api/ports.go:105-110`, on `UnitOfWork`: *\"⭐ IT IS WHAT MAKES A SOURCE AND ITS INGEST TOKEN ONE FACT. `createSource` writes to two tables owned by two modules — `alert_sources` here and `api_tokens` behind IngestTokenIssuer — and before this port existed they were two independent commits. A failure in the second left a source row that could never receive a webhook, which is worse than no source at all: the operator has a URL to paste and it answers 401 forever.\"* And `ports.go:97-99`, on `RevokeIngestTokens` itself: *\"Revokes every token scoped to the source. Deleting a source that could still be pushed to would be a soft delete in name only.\"*\n\n`deleteSource` is the inverse of the create-path bug that port was introduced to fix, in the same file, and it was not converted. The neighbouring handlers show the working pattern: `createSource` wraps seal-credential, create-source and mint-token in `rt.inTx` at `:159-174`, and `updateSource` wraps rotate-credential and update in `rt.inTx` at `:263-284`. `deleteSource` is the only write handler in the file with no `inTx`.\n\nThe handler's own doc-comment at `:292-296` states the intended guarantee: *\"It stops ingestion and reconciliation and REVOKES the ingest token, so a source that has been deleted cannot still be pushed to.\"* The code does not deliver it under partial failure.\n\n**Why it matters.** The residue is an authentication credential that outlives the resource it authenticates to, which is a security defect rather than a tidiness one: revocation that is only best-effort is not revocation. It is also silent — nothing in oto reports a token whose source is deleted, so the window is unbounded and closes only if someone re-runs the delete.\n\n**Where.** `internal/sources/api/sources.go:297-320` (`deleteSource`), `:159-174` and `:263-284` (the two handlers that do it correctly), `internal/sources/api/ports.go:87-100` (`IngestTokenIssuer`) and `:102-113` (`UnitOfWork`), `internal/app/container.go:857` (`Tx: sourceTx`, already wired).\n\n**Scope.** small\n\n**Done when.** `SoftDelete` and `RevokeIngestTokens` run inside one `rt.inTx`, and a test asserts that a failing `RevokeIngestTokens` leaves the source not soft-deleted and the transaction uncommitted — the shape `TestRotateTokenMintsBeforeItRevokes` already uses for the rotation path at `internal/sources/api/sources_guard_test.go:226-245`.","files":null}]}